@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Play a solo duel against a classmate
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Child" as actor
box "Frontend — game" #E0F2FE
  participant "DuelPage" as page
  participant "SoloGame" as solo
end box
box "Frontend — domain" #E0F2FE
  participant "ClassFactory" as factory
  participant "ClassmateAgent" as agent
  participant "Tour" as tour
  participant "Duel" as duel
end box
actor -> solo : "Go!" starts the solo game (no backend request, L2-019 criterion 1)
solo -> factory : build(picked kid, tour length, setup)
factory --> solo : Four kids not picked plus further classmates (L2-019 criterion 3, L2-020 criterion 1)
solo -> tour : Create tour, the device's player as traveller, desk 1 empty (L2-007 criteria 3 and 4)
tour --> solo : First duel, at desk 2, and its flash card
solo --> page : DuelState
page --> actor : Flash card
solo -> agent : decide(card)
agent -> agent : Answer and time from skill, characteristics, preferred maths
agent --> solo : ClassmateDecision, afterMs at or above 800 ms (to confirm)
solo -> solo : Schedule the classmate's answer on the game's clock
alt the child answers correctly first
  actor -> page : Answer
  page -> solo : answer(value)
  solo -> duel : answer(player, value, now)
  duel --> solo : Player wins (L2-001)
  solo -> solo : Clear the classmate's timer
else the classmate's time comes first
  solo -> duel : answer(classmate, value, now)
  alt the classmate's answer is correct
    duel --> solo : Classmate wins (L2-001)
  else the classmate's answer is wrong
    duel --> solo : Classmate frozen for 1 second (L2-020 criterion 4)
    solo -> agent : decide(card) again when the freeze ends
    agent --> solo : ClassmateDecision
    solo -> solo : Schedule the next answer
  end
end
solo -> tour : Read the tour after the duel
tour --> solo : TourState: hop, new traveller or end of tour
solo --> page : DuelState and TourState
page --> actor : Result of the duel, then World Map (L2-030 criterion 4)
@enduml
